From 1feab9778a7509b5a48ebc310160c2c021c1fe57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: the ADSP's audio PD over FastRPC; 64 MiB I/O map

FastRPC on the ADSP edge (third GLINK channel fastrpcglink-apps-dsp, pool
0xd3100000, SMMU streams 0x1803-0x1805, user PD): the 12 MiB remote heap at
0xd4000000 is zeroed and hyp-assigned (SCM MP_ASSIGN, HLOS -> LPASS +
ADSP_HEAP), createstaticpd "audiopd", then the listener the SLPI already had
(remotectl, apps_std) with files from /private/var/sweet/adsp-rpc/, before
the AFE steps. apps_std gains ftell, flen, rewind and feof; /vendor/lib/rfsa
paths map to the adsp dir; apps_mem is opened but only logged.

IO_MAP_SIZE is 64 MiB on SWEET: the 8 MiB submap ran out late in the boot and
io_map's KMA_NOFAIL panicked (0215c; the screen-off freezes of 0216c/0217).
The GLINK remote intent table holds 512 entries: the ADSP advertises dozens
of 0x80 intents per channel and 128 filled up before FastRPC got one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
